RPT#COMPRESS-355: {
 "summary": "Parsing PAX headers fails with NegativeArraySizeException"
 "description": "The TarArchiveInputStream.parsePaxHeaders method fails with a NegativeArraySizeException when there is an empty line at the end of the headers. The inner loop starts reading the length, but it gets a newline (10) and ends up subtracting '0' (48) from it; the result is a negative length that blows up an attempt to allocate the rest array. I would say that a check to see if ch is less the '0' and break the loop if it is."
}

